// Title: Sensitive File Access Via Volume Shadow Copy Backup
// Sigma ID: f57f8d16-1f39-4dcb-a604-6c73d9b54b3d
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Max Altgelt (Nextron Systems), Tobias Michalski (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-08-09 | Modified: 2024-01-18
// ATT&CK: impact, T1490
// Description: Detects a command that accesses the VolumeShadowCopy in order to extract sensitive files such as
//   the Security or SAM registry hives or the AD database (ntds.dit)
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/vxunderground/status/1423336151860002816?s=20
//   - https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/03e9b8c2e86d6db450e5eceec057d7e369ee2389b9daecaf06331a95410aa5f8/detection
//   - https://pentestlab.blog/2018/07/04/dumping-domain-password-hashes/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_susp_sensitive_file_access_shadowcopy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "\\\\?\\GLOBALROOT\\Device\\HarddiskVolumeShadowCopy" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "\\NTDS.dit" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\SYSTEM" or ProcessCommandLine contains "\\SECURITY")
